const posts = [
 {slug:'how-to-make-a-gift-hamper',title:'How to make a gift hamper at home: a thoughtful step-by-step guide',summary:'Choose a theme, plan the contents, build a stable arrangement and finish it with a personal message.',topic:'Make a hamper',minutes:7,image:'personalised-gift-hamper-inspiration.webp',takeaways:['Choose a recipient and occasion before shopping.','Arrange the contents before you buy the basket or box.','Protect food, glass and scented items for safe presentation and delivery.'],sections:[
  {heading:'1. Start with the recipient, not the basket',paragraphs:['A memorable hamper feels as if it was made for one person. Begin with the occasion and what the recipient enjoys: a quiet tea break, a new home, a birthday, a new job or a festive celebration. That gives you a simple theme to guide every later choice.','Write down one main item and two or three smaller additions that belong with it. For a tea theme, that might mean tea, a snack and a cup. For a new-home gift, consider a useful everyday item with a small treat and a note. A short, coherent list usually looks more considered than a box filled with unrelated things.']},
  {heading:'2. Set the budget and check practical details',paragraphs:['Decide your total spend before browsing. Include the container, protective filler, ribbon or wrap, message card and delivery materials, as well as the gifts themselves. If you are making several hampers, multiply each per-person cost and keep a little room for breakage or substitutions.','Check food labels, best-before dates, dietary needs and common allergens with care. Keep food sealed and away from candles, fragrance and other scented items. If you do not know the recipient’s restrictions, choose clearly labelled products and avoid making health or dietary promises.']},
  {heading:'3. Choose a base that fits the contents',paragraphs:['Lay the items out on a table and measure the footprint and tallest item. Then choose a sturdy box, tray or basket that leaves enough room for cushioning without making the contents look lost. A shallow base makes it easier to see each item; a deeper box needs more support so things do not slide.','If the hamper will be carried or shipped, favour a base that can be closed or wrapped securely. Check that the bottom is strong enough for the heaviest item. Glass jars need individual cushioning and should not press against one another.']},
  {heading:'4. Build the arrangement before wrapping',paragraphs:['Add a layer of filler, then place the heaviest items low and towards the back. Stand taller items behind shorter ones, and turn labels towards the person opening the hamper. Use small pieces of filler to keep items upright and to prevent movement.','Step back and look at the arrangement from the front and from above. Remove anything that blocks another item or makes the hamper feel crowded. Try a simple colour plan, such as kraft and green or cream with one festive accent, and repeat those colours in the card or ribbon.']},
  {heading:'5. Add a personal finish and check it can travel',paragraphs:['Write a short message that says why you chose the gift. A name tag or a ribbon in a favourite colour can add warmth without adding clutter. Keep the note easy to read and place it where it will be seen first.','Before handing it over, gently tilt the base to check that nothing shifts. Secure the lid or outer wrap, protect fragile corners and add an outer shipping carton if it is travelling. For a larger order, assemble one sample first, photograph the approved arrangement and use it as the packing reference.']}
 ],related:['hamperia','hampers']},
 {slug:'hamper-budget-checklist',title:'Gift hamper budget guide: plan the full cost before you buy',summary:'A practical way to price the container, gifts, finishing details and delivery without losing sight of the recipient.',topic:'Plan a budget',minutes:6,image:'creative-gift-wrapping-inspiration.webp',takeaways:['Set a per-gift ceiling and a total project budget.','Compare complete contents and quantities, not just the headline price.','Get customisation, shipping and delivery terms in the written quote.'],sections:[
  {heading:'Set a per-person target and a total',paragraphs:['For a personal gift, choose the total you are comfortable spending. For a team or client order, decide the per-recipient amount and multiply it by the number of gifts. Keep these two figures visible while comparing options so a small upgrade does not quietly change the overall budget.','Reserve part of the total for packaging, a message card, custom branding, shipping and any separate assembly charge. Ask whether the listed price is the finished hamper or an individual component. Hamperia’s supplies are sold as individual items; only products described as hampers are complete combinations.']},
  {heading:'Price the contents and presentation together',paragraphs:['List the main gift, supporting items, base, filler and finishing details. Record the quantity and unit price of each. A neat three-item collection can look more intentional than a larger assortment, and fewer items make it easier to keep the presentation stable.','Compare what is actually included. Check jar count, pack size, item quantity and whether the pictured card or decoration is part of the offer. For a customised order, ask for the final contents and any substitutions to be written into the quote.']},
  {heading:'Account for branding and quantity',paragraphs:['For corporate orders, ask which branding method suits the material: a card, sleeve, tag or printed item may each have different costs and minimum quantities. Share a clear logo file and approve the placement before production. Personalised names can require a separate list and additional checking.','Ask for prices at the quantities you are considering. Some costs change with volume, while individual delivery addresses or different gift variants can add handling work. Confirm the number of each variant rather than relying on an estimated total.']},
  {heading:'Confirm the final total before you commit',paragraphs:['Request one written total that identifies the contents, quantity, customisation, packing, shipping and payment schedule. Confirm the delivery locations and required arrival date. Ask whether taxes or other charges are included instead of assuming they are.','For Hamperia’s listed dry-fruit boxes, the current catalogue shows ₹699 for two glass jars, ₹1,099 for three and ₹1,499 for four. Check the live product page for the final assortment, weights, availability and current terms before ordering.']},
  {heading:'Keep a simple comparison sheet',paragraphs:['A small table helps you compare options fairly: product name, per-gift price, number of pieces, personalisation, delivery, lead time and final total. Add a column for the recipient and occasion so you do not choose on price alone.','If a preferred item may be unavailable, ask for an agreed alternative and its price in advance. That keeps the budget and presentation predictable if a substitution is needed.']}
 ],related:['shop-by-budget','corporate-gifting','dry-fruit-hampers']},
 {slug:'corporate-gifting-planning-checklist',title:'Corporate gifting guide: plan thoughtful gifts for employees and clients',summary:'Compare corporate gift ideas and prepare a clear brief for quantity, budget, branding and delivery.',topic:'Corporate gifting',minutes:7,image:'executive-corporate-planner-coffee-gift-box.webp',takeaways:['Separate audiences and confirm policies before choosing gifts.','Share quantity, budget, branding and delivery details in one brief.','Approve the final item list and artwork before production.'],sections:[
  {heading:'1. Define the purpose and recipients',paragraphs:['Start by writing down what the gift should communicate: welcome a new colleague, thank a client, recognise a milestone or mark a festive occasion. The purpose helps you choose between practical merchandise, a food-led hamper or a small keepsake with a personal message.','Separate employee, client and partner recipients when their preferences, policies or delivery plans differ. Check any company rules about gifts, value limits or food before selecting items. For food gifts, plan how ingredient and allergen information will be shared.']},
  {heading:'2. Prepare a complete enquiry brief',paragraphs:['Include the occasion, recipient count, budget per person, total budget, preferred items, required date and delivery locations. Add whether you want branded packaging, logo-ready merchandise, individual name cards or a consistent note. This information makes a quotation easier to understand and compare.','For apparel, estimate sizes and colours. For drinkware and merchandise, provide the logo artwork and any placement preferences. If you do not yet know every address, share the likely number of destinations and confirm when the final list will be ready.']},
  {heading:'3. Choose the right kind of gift',paragraphs:['A useful workday item such as a notebook or bottle can suit onboarding and team recognition. A curated hamper can mark a celebration or client milestone. A combination of branded merchandise and a small treat may work well for an event, provided the packaging can protect every item.','Keep the range manageable. Too many choices can make approvals, packing and distribution harder. If you need different gifts for different recipient groups, state each group’s quantity and budget clearly.']},
  {heading:'4. Review contents, artwork and price',paragraphs:['Check the full contents list, quantities and final product images. Ask which branding method is available for each material and request a proof for approval. Review names, spelling, dates, logo proportions and message text before signing off.','Ask for a complete quote that shows the gifts, packaging, branding, assembly, delivery and payment terms. Confirm whether prices are final and whether shipping or other charges are included. Hamperia product pages describe the current listed options; customised corporate work is confirmed by quotation.']},
  {heading:'5. Plan fulfilment and keep a record',paragraphs:['Confirm who will receive the shipment, how many parcels are expected and when the gifts need to arrive. For multiple addresses, agree a secure process for sharing recipient details. Leave time for production, packing and a check of quantities before the event.','Keep the approved contents, artwork, quote and delivery plan together. If a product must be substituted, confirm the replacement and any price change before it is packed. After delivery, reconcile the quantity received with the approved order.']}
 ],related:['corporate-gifting','employee-gifts','client-gifts','corporate-merchandise']}
];
